        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C. Any unit member dissatisfied with an adverse reclassification which results in a pay reduction or downgrading may appeal directly to the superintendent whose decision shall be final. A unit member assigned to a lower grade classification as a result of a reclassification will be placed on the lower pay grade without reduction in pay. When the same rate of pay does not exist in the lower pay grade, the unit member's hourly rate of pay will be red-circled which will remain in effect for no more than three (3) years from the effective date of the reclassification action. The unit member's anniversary date for step increases will not be affected.",
            "block_bbox": [
